{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB14488 - MONDO_1639",
  "verbalization": "Ferrous Gluconate is associated with Deficiency Anemia through a chain of indications that link it to Iron Deficiency Anemia and then to Deficiency Anemia. This pathway suggests that Ferrous Gluconate, which is used to treat Iron Deficiency Anemia, may indirectly contribute to the development of Deficiency Anemia in some cases. The evidence is supported by the shared indication of Iron Deficiency Anemia between Ferrous Gluconate and Ferumoxytol, a drug that is also indicated for Deficiency Anemia. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where Ferrous Gluconate may influence iron metabolism, potentially leading to a deficiency in iron and subsequent anemia. The recurring role of Iron Deficiency Anemia as a mediator underscores the importance of this intermediate step in the relationship between Ferrous Gluconate and Deficiency Anemia.",
